it's the first positive move in five  years between Ukraine and Russia a  filmmaker and a group of sailors landed  in Kiev Airport in a long anticipated  prisoner swap the release of Ukrainian  filmmaker oleg sentsov who was jailed  for 22 years is seen as a major  concession by russia and president  Vladimir's olenski fulfilled his  election promise to bring home 22  ukrainian sailors and two security  service agents we have to do all the  steps to finish this horrible war I  think the sailors on board three  Ukrainian vessels were captured here in  the Kerch Strait nine months ago after  Russian warships opened fire on them  the Kremlin says they illegally entered  Russian waters near the Crimean  Peninsula which Russian troops seized  and annexed from Ukraine in 2014  since then the Kremlin backed  separatists have been at war with  Ukrainian government forces in eastern  Ukraine at least 10,000 people have been  killed since the fighting began five  years ago Ukraine's recently elected  president zalenski says he wants to  revive peace negotiations with Russia  he's been seeking support from European  leaders recently and he spoken to  President Vladimir Putin by phone the  prisoner exchange could be an important  step towards further tentative talks the  swap is being seen as a victory for both  presidents Putin and zalenski a  potential suspect and witness in the  downing of the Malaysian Airlines jet  over Ukraine five years ago has also  been released despite protests by the  Dutch government who had many of its  citizens on the flight that suggests the  Lenski not only had to make concessions  but that Russia will be a tough  negotiating partner in future talks to  end fighting in eastern Ukraine Victoria  Gaytan be al-jazeera
 

